        "text": "Eira Lizeth Corral Sepúlveda has served as an MWRD commissioner since 2020 and previously was the village clerk of Hanover Park from 2009 to 2021. She chairs the Monitoring & Research and Municipalities committees. Her work focuses on managing regional stormwater, improving water quality, and preventing flooding. She supports the MWRD’s Restore the Canopy program, which provides free native tree saplings to residents and schools.",
